In article <18148@helios.TAMU.EDU> z0w3116@venus.tamu.edu writes:
>How to survive the frozen attack? 
>
>Most of my good characters were killed by frozen attack. A Babarian was killed
>by the sleep ray of an orange dragon, a Priest by something I don't know 
>(probably air elemental). My last character, a Wizard, was killed by a 
>stupid gelatinous cube.
>
>Does sleep resistance prevent from be frozen?

You've encountered two different kinds of freezing: sleeping and paralysis.
An orange dragon and (e.g.) homunculus put you to sleep. If you are sleep
resistant, this won't work for the monsters. Also there is a sleeping gas
trap which puts you to sleep, but if you are resistant to it, you'll walk
in an gas cloud with no effects.
A gelatinous cube and (e.g.) a guardian Naga paralysis you. Sleep resistance
does not prevent this. I don't think there is anything against getting
paralysed, except stay out of the way of these monsters :-)
